<RESOLUTION><CREATED>1793730585</CREATED>
<DESC><![CDATA[[b]Understanding[/b] that sizable standing forces held by governments waste public funds and can be used against member nations,

[b]Recognizing[/b] that defense of the nation should be in the hands of proportional forces backed up by reserve forces and voluntary civilian defense organizations,

[b]Understanding[/b] that threatened states need to have some way of defending themselves,

The World Assembly, consistent with prior World Assembly laws which still apply in regard to the following issues,

1. [b]Defines[/b], for the purposes of this resolution:
 a. &quot;[i]state[/i]&quot; to mean a member nation or any administrative subdivision of the nation;
 b. &quot;[i]standing force[/i]&quot; to mean any group of individuals who are employed as a full time professional by the state and are engaged in armed or combat support operations, and are not police, civilian first responders, reserves or militia; and
 c. &quot;[i]emergency[/i]&quot; to mean the period when a state is under armed assault or there is a credible and immediate threat of armed invasion;

2. [b]Prohibits[/b], outside of an emergency, any member nation from maintaining standing forces in the aggregate that exceed one percent of the population governed by the member nation;

3. [b]Holds[/b] that the prohibition in clause 2 shall not apply during the period of emergency and for ninety days after the end of such emergency, and is exempted from the prohibitions in clause 2 in relation to any standing forces that are engaged in activities authorized by prior World Assembly resolutions and laws;

4. [b]Requires[/b] that any member nation who holds standing forces in excess of the amount specified in clause 2, must reduce those forces to comply with clause 2 within ten years by either attrition or voluntarily leaving service;

5. [b]Holds[/b] that nothing in this resolution:
 a. places limitations on the weapons, equipment and technology available to the state;
 b. sets limits on the size of the police force, reserves or militia;
 c. prevents any person from joining a reserve or a militia, or a voluntary defense organization;

6. [b]Recommends[/b] member nations provide support for civilian volunteer defense organizations.]]></DESC>
